  message: "PREMISE RE-CHECK 2026-09-29 on dev 6929699126: CURRENT, and worse than filed; the denominator drifted. Code unchanged since WI-sakir (2a92c2a650): ts_def_use.py:348 _JSTS_FUNCTION_NODE_TYPES = {function_declaration, method_definition}; ddg_build.py:244 walks only those.\nREPRO: host_secret -> network, all three sharing symbol id javascript:app.js:1-5:handler:function -- function handler -> VIOLATED ddg/confirmed; const handler = (url) => {} and a function expression -> VIOLATED structural/unavailable.\nIT CAUSES FALSE POSITIVES, not only lost precision (reproduced twice, by the re-check agent and independently by me): the key is read and only its length logged, fetch(url) sends no secret. function declaration -> CONFIRMED (0 flows); the same body as an arrow -> VIOLATED, structural/unavailable.\ndash.js re-measured (survey 212 s; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/premise_09292026/mufag/), span-matching symbols to tree-sitter node types: 3,981 of 7,592 JS callable SYMBOLS never walked (arrow 2,000 vs filed 2,001; function_expression 1,981 vs filed 3,515). Counting syntactic function nodes: 4,902 of 8,510. The filed 11,600 denominator did not reproduce with this instrument (the filing's instrument was a spy on ddg_build._solve_one_function, not span-matching). apollo-server and the \"TS 0 sinks\" clause were not re-checked."  # 1174
