- op: discuss  # d967
  at: '2026-09-29T11:10:12Z'  # d967
  by: agent  # d967
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d967
  clock: 4  # d967
  nonce: d967  # d967
  message: "FIXED in PR #1299 (merged, dev c796fc6258). LanguageDdgSpec gains bound_callable_node_types (JS/TS: arrow_function, function_expression, function, generator_function). Such a node is walked ONLY under the id the ANALYZER emitted at its exact span: ddg_build.analyzer_symbol_index over the survey nodes verify-claims already holds, keyed (language, path, start line, start col, end line); a span two symbols share is dropped, not guessed. No name is re-derived in the DDG -- js_ts names these callables half a dozen ways (handler, _cb_<callee>@<col>, _iife), and a second copy would drift.\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE on merged dev (the premise-check repro): key read, only its length logged, unrelated fetch(url) -- function declaration CONFIRMED, the same body as `const handler = (url) => {}` now CONFIRMED (was VIOLATED structural/unavailable). A real leak in an arrow or a function expression reads VIOLATED ddg/confirmed (test_js_binding_named_callables_are_walked, 6 cases; mutation of the registration turns 4 red).\nMEASURED (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/mufag_09292026/): dash.js DDG walked symbols 2,315 -> 4,275, DDG build 7.3 s -> 10.6 s (direct timing; the 262 s -> 557 s verify-claims wall clock in the A/B log was concurrent-load noise). Verdict A/B dash.js, growthbook, apollo-server: 0 verdicts changed; dash.js 1 of 3 and apollo-server 1 of 3 findings moved off structural; growthbook unchanged (43 structural) -- its code is mostly .tsx, which the typescript spec's *.ts glob does not reach (the WI-fovus family). unleash/koel A/B still running at close; not asserted.\nNOT ASSERTED: that an expression-bodied arrow (x => f(x)) yields DDG edges -- its body is an expression, not a statement block; walked if the CFG builder handles it, otherwise it keeps the structural arm."  # d967
